Interview Question
Why do we use Environment Variables?

Answer:

Environment Variables are used to store configuration and sensitive information outside the source code, such as URLs, usernames, passwords, API keys, and tokens. They improve security, support multiple environments, reduce hardcoding, and make automation frameworks easier to maintain.

Interview Question
What is process.env?

Answer:

process.env is a Node.js object that provides access to environment variables loaded from the operating system or .env files. In Playwright frameworks, it is commonly used to access configuration values such as base URLs, credentials, and API keys.

Real Project Example

Instead of:

TypeScript
await page.goto(
'https://qa.orangehrm.com'
);

Use:

TypeScript
await page.goto(
process.env.BASE_URL!
);

Now if the project moves from QA to UAT:

Plain Text
QA URL → Change .env only
UAT URL → Change .env only

✅ No code changes required.

One-line Interview Answer

Environment Variables help externalize configuration and sensitive data from the automation code, enabling secure, maintainable, and environment-independent test execution. 🚀